    "defect_analysis": "Swayam WAS actively included in the recovery candidate similarity comparison set evaluated for Track 20 at frame 1230, despite Track 10 still actively holding ownership of 'swayam' (Track 10 was in LOST state, unevicted until frame 1232). Track 20 narrowly avoided an immediate duplicate-ownership collision only because Aagam's embedding score happened to exceed Swayam's embedding score (0.7522 vs 0.6246). A different noise draw could have allowed Swayam to win, resulting in an unmitigated duplicate active ownership violation. This confirms a genuine code-level near-miss defect in candidate scoping: BodyGallery.search and robust_tracker.py query all enrolled students unconditionally rather than filtering strictly to genuinely unowned/missing students.",
    "code_defect_location": {
      "features_py_line_219": "BodyGallery.search iterates over self._galleries.items() unconditionally with zero missing/unowned filtering.",
      "robust_tracker_py_line_238": "Calls self.body_gallery.top_match(body_emb) without passing an unowned candidate whitelist.",
      "identity_lock_manager_py_lines_268_299": "attempt_gap_recovery lacks candidate pool pre-filtering against student_owner."
    }
  },
